<title>UK: Nickel ends LME kerb sharply lower, others soft.</title>
<headline>Nickel ends LME kerb sharply lower, others soft.</headline>
<text>
<p>NICKEL - Dives after fails to sustain move to fresh nine-month high. Ends sharply lower at $7,850.</p>
<p>COPPER - Finishes weaker at $2,350. Cash/threes narrower.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Softer under $1,651 chart point.</p>
<p>ZINC - Easier, moves back towards $1,200. LEAD - Edges lower. TIN - Ends just above $5,900. ALLOY - Weaker with primary.</p>
</text>
